# Divergent per-chip TMC SPI register state. Two TMC SPI chips share
# the same bus (tmc2130 stepper_x on PG0 and tmc5160 stepper_y on
# PG1); a write to one chip's CHOPCONF must not poison the other
# chip's read. Real hardware enforces this because each chip is its
# own physical register file; the bridge enforces it by keying its
# 5-byte register table off the active CS pin, with each chip
# registered via spi_tmc_chip on init.
#
# Requires the emulator backend: under the fileoutput fallback,
# klippy's DUMP_TMC sees the all-zero DummyResponse and the per-chip
# state can't be observed.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
EMULATOR tmc_spi_divergence.fixture.json
CONFIG tmc_spi.cfg
REQUIRES_EMULATOR

# Set distinct toff values on stepper_x (tmc2130) and stepper_y
# (tmc5160). klippy writes its full local CHOPCONF cache (with the
# requested toff) to each chip in turn; without per-chip tables the
# second write would overwrite the first in a single shared CHOPCONF
# slot, and both DUMP_TMCs below would read back toff=8. With
# per-chip tables each chip retains its own value.
SET_TMC_FIELD STEPPER=stepper_x FIELD=toff VALUE=3
SET_TMC_FIELD STEPPER=stepper_y FIELD=toff VALUE=8
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_y

# pretty_format prints each non-zero CHOPCONF field as " toff=N" -
# both values must appear in the log (each from its own chip's dump).
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "toff=3"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "toff=8"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "TMC stepper_x failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "TMC stepper_y failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU"
